From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:38:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 091/104] text: shape with HarfBuzz and take WE's font fallback
 chain
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WE shapes each line with HarfBuzz (GH 0x1401da3c0 cuts it into runs of one face and shapes each),
so GPOS kerning, ligatures and marks apply; LWE placed FreeType glyphs with the legacy kern table
only, which most fonts (NotoSans among them) don't have: their texts came out too wide (B4: 34 of
50 literal texts within 3 % of the editor's saved width). A line is now cut into runs as WE cuts it
(each character's face from the fallback chain; tab, LF, CR, space and ZWJ stay in the run before
them), each run shaped by hb_shape on an hb_ft font of its face, advances x_advance >> 6, offsets
applied. The control-character skip is kept.

A character the font lacks goes to WE's fallback chain (the table at 0x1404c5030, in order):
arial.ttf, seguiemj.ttf, arialuni.ttf, segoeui.ttf, WE's own fonts/TwemojiMozilla.ttf,
seguisym.ttf, msyh.ttc, Malgun.ttf. Each Windows file is looked up by its family, then the
families fontconfig commonly has in its place (Liberation Sans/Arimo, Noto Emoji, Noto Sans,
Selawik, Noto Sans Symbols 2, Noto Sans CJK SC/KR …; a substitute is accepted only under that
exact family name); TwemojiMozilla is read from WE's assets. fontconfig's own best font stays as a
last resort (ours: a Windows system has every slot's font).

Inferred: the hb_ft font with HarfBuzz's default load flags, script and direction guessed per run
(WE's run builder FUN_1401e1c00 / 0x1401e0eb0 wasn't read past the split).

Links harfbuzz (pkg-config).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md "Leftovers result" (B4's shaping and fallback chain)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
